title: Storybook3
---
<<bg thorn_layers_fullscreen>>
Gardener: The sun's out today, would you like to see? Your fort is so dense, light can't beam through the seams.
Rose: Nothing worth seeing, a world of pain and depleting. I was born on a battlefield, with no way of leaving.
Gardener: You can't see the change that the land has undergone. Where once it was barren, there are flowers and lawn.
Gardener: Your armor's rendered you pale; you're a stranger to lush. Shrouded in your own darkness, your hopes are surely hushed.
Rose: War will dawn again. Why hope when peace is just a ploy?
Gardener: What is it you're surviving for, if not awaiting joy? Let me provide you with a peephole through which to know the land.
Rose: What joy is worth my weakness? You can keep away your hands.
Narrator: The gardener accompanied her in silence. Though this silence was quite loud.
Narrator: Would she ever pull her punches? And if ever, why not now?
Rose: My thorns often puncture me; bring me pain if I am honest. I could slacken at my leash, lead a life more filled with promise.
Narrator: The gardener obliged her resolution, pruned her edges with great care.
Gardener: I'm grateful the thorns have delivered you, but it's time for them to share.
<<bg thorn_layers_3_layers>>
Narrator: The sky came into focus, and rays of light embraced her face.
Narrator: Just a little was enough for now; she would do things at her pace.
<<end>>
===